        "excerpt": "An inherited \"no-rebuild\" property is not unsellable, but its pricing and sale differ from an ordinary lot. Article 43 of the Building Standards Act requires the site to front a road for at least 2 metres; the \"road\" is defined by Article 42. Even where frontage falls short, there are routes — setback, buying adjacent land, and the certification or permission under Article 43(2). A licensed real estate agent and administrative scrivener in Bunkyo, Tokyo sets out what to confirm before you sell.",
